      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It would be really good to have a more finely grained friendship system yes.\n\nLike, \"acquaintances\", \"followers\", \"special friends\", with various permissions sets for each . For instance a follower could only find you and join you if you are blue, but they cannot see if you are online or not if you are not blue. An acquaintance could join you if you are blue, but would still have to request if you are green. They would be able to see if you are online, though. Special friends would be able to join you when you are green, without asking.\n\nI see this very useful for content creators, djs, hosts, event organisers, dancers, etc etc. Right now we have to constantly hide behind an alt or orange status to be able to enjoy some moments with close friends without being joined or asked by people who we friended only for the purposes of events or content promotion. It hinders our true friends from joining us, and I think it is quite unfair.\n\nI hear people saying \"oh yes but then people will bitch because they won't like being just an acquaintance\", but I think that is simply what happens for all kind of people with some exposure. Usually we don't have our favourite singer's or actor's email or phone number right ?  But we can still follow them on social media.\n\nMaybe \"contacts\" would be a nicer way to say it.\n\nWith vrc being a highly social platform, I think this basic feature is really missing.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
