      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would would be amazing. The current system just causes a slew of orange users, including myself, because of people that I add as CONTACTS, that I can visit again, but I do NOT want them joining me at will on green. This is ridiculous and long over due for a overhaul. The friend system needs to change.\n\nI'd argue there's already a poor implementation with orange status also hiding what world I'm in? Why does orange status also behave like i'm in a private instance. I set myself on orange to stop people from joining WIHTOUT ASKING, not to hide what I'm doing, that's what private instances are for. \n\nAt best you MUST separate JOIN permission from visibility. We should have 2 statuses. 1. Join freely/not freely & 2. World visible/not visible. Separate the function.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
